### kafka-wallet — runnable request collection
# IntelliJ HTTP Client or the VS Code "REST Client" extension.
# Run them top to bottom; later requests reuse ids captured from earlier ones.

@wallet = http://localhost:8080
@notifications = http://localhost:8081
@fraud = http://localhost:8082

### Open Alice's account
# @name openAlice
POST {{wallet}}/accounts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ownerName": "Alice",
  "initialBalance": "1000.00",
  "currency": "BRL"
}

> {% client.global.set("alice", response.body.id); %}

### Open Bob's account
# @name openBob
POST {{wallet}}/accounts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ownerName": "Bob",
  "initialBalance": "0.00",
  "currency": "BRL"
}

> {% client.global.set("bob", response.body.id); %}

### Transfer — expect 201 Created
# @name transfer
POST {{wallet}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-001

{
  "fromAccountId": "{{alice}}",
  "toAccountId": "{{bob}}",
  "amount": "150.00",
  "currency": "BRL"
}

> {% client.global.set("transferId", response.body.transferId); %}

### Replay the exact same request — expect 200 OK, same transferId, no money moved
POST {{wallet}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-001

{
  "fromAccountId": "{{alice}}",
  "toAccountId": "{{bob}}",
  "amount": "150.00",
  "currency": "BRL"
}

### Same key, different amount — expect 409 Conflict (idempotency-key-reused)
POST {{wallet}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-001

{
  "fromAccountId": "{{alice}}",
  "toAccountId": "{{bob}}",
  "amount": "151.00",
  "currency": "BRL"
}

### Alice's balance — expect 850.0000
GET {{wallet}}/accounts/{{alice}}

### Bob's balance — expect 150.0000
GET {{wallet}}/accounts/{{bob}}

### Alice's ledger — one DEBIT per transfer she sent
GET {{wallet}}/accounts/{{alice}}/ledger?limit=20

### Bob's ledger — the matching CREDIT
GET {{wallet}}/accounts/{{bob}}/ledger?limit=20

### The transfer itself
GET {{wallet}}/transfers/{{transferId}}

### Overdraft — expect 422 (insufficient-funds)
POST {{wallet}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-overdraft

{
  "fromAccountId": "{{alice}}",
  "toAccountId": "{{bob}}",
  "amount": "999999.00",
  "currency": "BRL"
}

### Transfer to self — expect 422 (same-account-transfer)
POST {{wallet}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-self

{
  "fromAccountId": "{{alice}}",
  "toAccountId": "{{alice}}",
  "amount": "10.00",
  "currency": "BRL"
}

### More than 4 decimal places — expect 400 from bean validation
POST {{wallet}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-precision

{
  "fromAccountId": "{{alice}}",
  "toAccountId": "{{bob}}",
  "amount": "10.000001",
  "currency": "BRL"
}

### Missing Idempotency-Key — expect 400
POST {{wallet}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fromAccountId": "{{alice}}",
  "toAccountId": "{{bob}}",
  "amount": "10.00",
  "currency": "BRL"
}

### Above the fraud threshold — watch fraud.alert in the Kafka UI
POST {{wallet}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-big-{{$timestamp}}

{
  "fromAccountId": "{{bob}}",
  "toAccountId": "{{alice}}",
  "amount": "10000.00",
  "currency": "BRL"
}

### How many notifications were sent — one per transfer, never two
GET {{notifications}}/notifications/count

### Notifications for one transfer
GET {{notifications}}/notifications/by-transfer/{{transferId}}

### --- Observability ---

### Outbox backlog — 0 when the relay has caught up
GET {{wallet}}/actuator/metrics/wallet.outbox.backlog

### Transfers created vs. replayed
GET {{wallet}}/actuator/metrics/wallet.transfers

### Consumer outcomes: processed / duplicate / dead-lettered
GET {{notifications}}/actuator/metrics/notification.events

### Health of each service
GET {{wallet}}/actuator/health

###
GET {{notifications}}/actuator/health

###
GET {{fraud}}/actuator/health

### --- Failure injection (needs notification.failure-injection.enabled=true) ---

### Fail every delivery — the message ends up in transfer.completed.dlq
POST {{notifications}}/test/failure-injection?mode=ALWAYS

### Fail twice then succeed — retry recovering
POST {{notifications}}/test/failure-injection?mode=TRANSIENT&times=2

### Back to normal
POST {{notifications}}/test/failure-injection?mode=NONE
